{"data":{"body":"**P1 \u2014 Clarify that fail-fast does not cancel in-flight branches.** The executor stops scheduling pending branches after observing a failure, but already-started branches continue; with the default unlimited concurrency, every branch may be submitted before that failure is observed. The current wording can lead users to assume side-effecting branches will not run. Document the in-flight behavior and recommend `max_concurrency` when users need to bound it.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPsIIsM7obUv-","finding_digest":"ed1610006a8ae2935a558f826667534828620778e3d6a034523dc4577c53170e","finding_id":"arf_v1_5ulbaadkrlrjgwsvr6bgmz2tja","finding_key":"docs/migration-1.x-to-2.x.md::default-map-parallel-completion::in-flight-branches-not-cancelled","identity_key":"docs/migration-1.x-to-2.x.md::default-map-parallel-completion::in-flight-branches-not-cancelled","line":8,"observation_digest":"34ad4c0eb8cd7a3686585cf461a4e459be79be3e38274cc39de187be014877a5","observation_id":"aro_v1_gswuydvyzv5dnbsylt2gdjhelg","path":"docs/migration-1.x-to-2.x.md","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-08-31T23:49:44Z","review_id":"arr_v1_tfr6jxz6qkaygiymzcf7ou7f5x","reviewed_base_sha":"ae73e73a9749d8faf73fc5530ce0429a70a5a725","reviewed_head_sha":"0edb4a66576ce163f99abf202035da6a37c1cec3","reviewer":"codex","start_line":7,"suggestion_id":"arsg_v1_jctb7yooxtc6qvmi6afi7qjsoc"},"pull_request":{"number":655},"record_id":"art_v1_5a6wclx3gikquwukeeyw75ew5i","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-08-31T23:49:44Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python","id":1052903600},"schema_version":1}
